apps
# `agents` and `sandbox` stay in context: patchapi-agents declares
# `package = false`, so the Change Intelligence image imports the fleet from
# source rather than installing it. Together they are under 1.5 MB.
# demo is 1.3 GB of pinned checkouts. The provider notices inside it are 16 KB
# and the agent lane cannot read a change without them. The exclusion is on the
# children rather than the directory so the exception can re-include one.
demo/*
!demo/fixtures
docs
infra
# `skills` stays in context. The patch stage reads a provider migration skill
# before it plans, and the skill is where the capability differences live — the
# part that makes a migration more than a string replacement. Two directories,
# well under a megabyte.
tests
db
artifacts
sandbox-workspaces
tmp-patchapi
*.md
!packages/**/README.md
!services/**/README.md
# A skill *is* markdown — SKILL.md is the file `load_migration_skill` reads.
!skills/**/*.md
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
